# THE DETECTOR SEAM.
#
# Every grasp source — analytic, GPD, GraspGen — advertises exactly this service, so
# grasp_source:=analytic|gpd|graspgen swaps the server and the MTC task does not change
# by one line. That is the whole point: the A/B between geometric candidate sampling
# (GPD) and diffusion generative (GraspGen) has to run the same executor, same gripper,
# same scene, or it measures nothing.

# --- request ---
# Coarse target position. In the mission this originates from the UAV detector (via
# /detected_targets); in the harness it comes from the color detector. Either way it is
# only a HINT — a 12 m-altitude detection is nowhere near grasp-accurate. The server is
# expected to refine it from its own sensing.
geometry_msgs/PointStamped target

# Optional segmented object cloud. Leave empty and the server captures its own.
# GPD needs this; the analytic server ignores it.
sensor_msgs/PointCloud2 cloud
---
# --- response ---
bool success
string message

# Ranked best-first. These are poses of **grasp_tcp** (the jaw center-line: +Z approach,
# +X finger closing), NOT of ur5_tool0. Any frame conversion belongs in the server, never
# downstream — that is exactly the mistake the legacy code made.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped[] grasps

# Required gripper opening at each grasp, metres. The 2F-140 spans 0.136 m (open) to
# ~0.008 m (closed); anything wider than the aperture must be filtered out by the server.
float32[] width

# Detector confidence, same order. The analytic server reports 1.0.
float32[] score
